      "writtenOn": "2024-01-08T21:24:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking about this a bit more, I think we can make it even clearer. Ultimately what we want to do in all of these tests is read `fpscr`. We\u0027re either reading it directly by calling `read_fpscr` or reading it when the FPU interrupt is triggered. In that case, I think it would make sense to call this function `read_fpscr` (and rename the other one something like `_read_fpscr`. Then this function becomes something like (some pseudocode here):\n\n```\n#if defined(CHIP_FAMILY_STM32F4) || defined(CHIP_FAMILY_STM32H7)\nstatic bool supports_fpu_irq \u003d true;\n#define FPU_IRQ STM32_IRQ_FPU\nstatic volatile bool fpu_irq_handled;\n#else\nstatic bool supports_fpu_irq \u003d false;\n#define FPU_IRQ -1\n#endif\n\nvoid read_fpscr(void)\n{\n  if (supports_fpu_irq)) {\n    if (STM32H7)\n      task_trigger_irq(FPU_IRQ);\n    while (!fpu_irq_handled) {}\n    return;\n  } \n  _read_fpscr();\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "cd3fc6a8cf9d947588b67f7307b59dc687a2c092",
